Exact mean-to-variance contraction for the same sign-conditioned law
==================================================================

Let p=P(X>0), q=1-p, v=pq, and let the conditional centered residual
variances be summarized in the existing count coordinates by s=lambda/n>=0.
For the one actual standardized marginal the signed first moment
m=E X_+=E X_- satisfies m=v/sqrt(v+s)>0. These are physical variables of
the same marginal, not independent moments from different optimizers.

Suppose an acquired interval gives 0<=ml<=m<=mh<=1/2. With 0<p<1,
mh=0 is impossible. Solving the identity gives

                  s = v^2/m^2 - v.

For fixed v>0 this expression decreases in m. Thus
 v^2/mh^2-v <= s,
and if ml>0 also s <= v^2/ml^2-v.
Further m^2<=v since s>=0, so v>=ml^2. On a closed actual probability
interval [pl,pu], v has minimum min(pl(1-pl),pu(1-pu)) and maximum1/4
when the interval contains1/2, otherwise its larger endpoint value.
Intersect this variance interval with [ml^2,infinity). An empty intersection
excludes the actual law. Otherwise the preceding inequalities imply

 lambda >= n min_{v in interval}(v^2/mh^2-v),
 lambda <= n max_{v in interval}(v^2/ml^2-v)  [if ml>0].

Both quadratics are convex. The lower minimum occurs at an endpoint or
the stationary point mh^2/2, when present. The upper maximum occurs at an
endpoint. Every quantity is rational, so there is no radical rounding or
numeric optimization. Intersect with the incoming closed lambda interval
and lambda>=0. A strict lower>upper is the only interval-empty test.
Equal endpoints are retained. The upper inequality is omitted if ml=0.
The reasoning covers both probability halves, the seam1/2, s=0 and any n>=1.

This is a necessary-condition contraction, not a converse moment-feasibility
result. It may be applied before other valid contractions in a finite sequence.
Every subsequent count leaf must still be recomputed on the surviving box;
the stored forest must reconstruct and cover its original full root boxes.
The acquired mean premise, and its same-law meaning, remain separate resource
and analytic obligations. This lemma does not supply either of them.
